{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-111121-r4514097","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Smoking Shrimp Creole","sourcePageId":111121,"sourceRevision":"4514097","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-19T01:43:00Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Smoking%20Shrimp%20Creole&oldid=4514097","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T16:17:33.011Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Boiled recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Main course recipes","Category:Naturally gluten-free recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using bay leaf","Category:Recipes using canola oil","Category:Recipes using celery","Category:Recipes using chipotle chile","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes using green bell pepper","Category:Recipes using rice","Category:Recipes using shrimp","Category:Recipes using tomato","Category:Southern U.S. recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"d00a4139354f7bd469e84378ebebba90c7796167ca9c70351d9f84e9245ce85d","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary|category=Seafood recipes|servings=4|time=1 hour|difficulty=2\n}}\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of the United States|American cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Southern cuisine|Southern U.S. cuisine]]\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Canola Oil|canola oil]]\n* ¾ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Chop|chopped]] [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]]\n* 1 small seeded [[Cookbook:Green Pepper|green bell pepper]]\n* 1 small [[Cookbook:Celery|celery]] rib, thinly sliced\n* 2 teaspoons finely chopped [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]]\n* 1 can (14 [[Cookbook:Ounce|ounces]]) crushed [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomatoes]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Bay Leaf|bay leaf]]\n* 1 teaspoon ground [[Cookbook:Paprika|paprika]]\n* ¼–½ ground [[Cookbook:Chipotle Chili|chipotle chili]]\n* ¾ [[Cookbook:Pound|pound]] small or medium [[Cookbook:shrimp|shrimp]], shelled\n* [[Cookbook:Salt|Salt]]\n* Freshly-ground [[Cookbook:Pepper|black pepper]]\n* 2 cups cooked long-grain [[Cookbook:Rice|brown rice]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Heat the oil in a medium [[Cookbook:Skillet|skillet]] over medium-high heat.\n# [[Cookbook:Sauté|Sauté]] the onion, celery, pepper, and garlic until the onion is translucent, 4–5 minutes.\n# Add the tomatoes, bay leaves, paprika, and chipotle chili.\n# [[Cookbook:Simmer|Simmer]] the sauce, uncovered, until it is thick, 15–20 minutes, stirring it 2–3 times.\n# Add the shrimp and cook, uncovered, until they are pink and firm, 5–7 minutes, depending on their size.\n# Season to taste with salt and pepper.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* Serve over cooked [[Cookbook:Rice|brown rice]].\n\n[[Category:Southern U.S. recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using shrimp]]\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using tomato]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Naturally gluten-free recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bay leaf]]\n[[Category:Recipes using green bell pepper]]\n[[Category:Recipes using celery]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chipotle chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using canola oil]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Smoking Shrimp Creole","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":